From: Marmalade STT <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Cancellable offline decodes for Whisper and Qwen3-ASR (#49)

Not upstream; ours. Patch 0002 left Whisper's greedy decoder free to run
up to its own 224-token limit, and a decode can't be interrupted from the
JNI: a runaway kept the app's engine busy for seconds after the user
cancelled. OfflineStream::Cancel() sets an atomic flag (thread-safe; the
JNI exposes it as OfflineStream.cancel). The autoregressive decoders
(Whisper's greedy search, Qwen3-ASR's generation loop, Canary's) check it
before every decoder step and stop with the tokens decoded so far; a
Whisper stream cancelled before its decode starts skips the encoder too. The encoder run itself still can't be
stopped.
---
--- a/sherpa-onnx/csrc/offline-recognizer-canary-impl.h
+++ b/sherpa-onnx/csrc/offline-recognizer-canary-impl.h
@@ -151,6 +151,12 @@
         break;
       }
 
+      // Marmalade STT (#49): a cancelled decode stops at the next step (the
+      // pop_back below then drops a real token, which nobody reads).
+      if (s->IsCancelled()) {
+        break;
+      }
+
       std::tie(logits, decoder_states) =
           RunDecoder(tokens.back(), i, std::move(decoder_states),
                      View(&enc_states), View(&enc_mask));
--- a/sherpa-onnx/csrc/offline-recognizer-qwen3-asr-impl.cc
